-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- 00655 — Pledge / commission-share copy out of three live email templates
--
-- The Pledge ("a quarter of our commission goes back to the designers who
-- teach the system") is legal-gated and must not appear in studio-facing
-- copy. It was carried by three of the 17 designer-onboarding templates:
--
--   designer-invite          (T0) — the "One promise up front" paragraph
--   onboarding-aesthete      (E9) — the "here is the part I'll always state
--                                   plainly" paragraph (incl. "paid work")
--   milestone-first-payment  (M4) — the "the Pledge stops being a line in a
--                                   welcome letter" paragraph, AND the
--                                   preview line "and the Pledge is now in
--                                   motion."
--
-- WHY A MIGRATION AND NOT A REDEPLOY: the send path renders from the
-- email_templates ROW, not from packages/email/src/templates/*.tsx
-- (supabase/functions/_shared/render-template.ts interpolates {{var}} into
-- html_content). Redeploying the designer-invite edge function is a no-op
-- for copy. The .tsx sources are the authoring surface and were edited in
-- the same commit; this migration carries the same bytes into the rows.
--
-- Lineage of these rows: 00293 (seed) → 00310 (branded reseed) → 00404
-- (td-padding re-bake) → this. 00293/00310/00404 are point-in-time
-- snapshots and are left untouched, per 00293's own header and
-- packages/email/scripts/render-db-templates.ts:20-22 ("re-run this script
-- and ship the refreshed SQL as a NEW migration").
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THE HTML BELOW: rendered by
-- `pnpm --filter @patina/email render:onboarding-templates` from the
-- edited .tsx, so row and source match byte-for-byte. Verified against
-- 00404: the other 14 templates re-render byte-identical (0 drift), which
-- proves the source tree matched the live rows before this change; the only
-- deltas here are the three removals above, plus — for M4 only —
-- react-email's automatic invisible preview padding (3 extra repeats of
-- U+FEFF U+00A0 U+200C U+200B U+200D U+200E U+200F), which shifts because
-- the new preview string is 3 characters shorter.
--
-- Metadata (name, description, category, subject_default, variables) is
-- byte-identical for all three and is deliberately NOT written here.
--
-- Idempotent: three unconditional UPDATEs keyed on the unique slug, no
-- DELETE, no INSERT. Reruns converge on the same bytes. The guard block at
-- the end fails loudly if a slug is missing or any promise phrase survives.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

UPDATE public.email_templates
   SET html_content = $html$<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd"><html dir="ltr" lang="en"><head><meta content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" http-equiv="Content-Type"/><meta name="x-apple-disable-message-reformatting"/><meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark"/><meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,500;0,9..144,600;1,9..144,400&amp;family=Hanken+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&amp;display=swap"/><style>:root { color-scheme: light dark; supported-color-schemes: light dark; }
